foundation.question_text:
Name the solid that folds up from this net.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.7]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (2,3);
\draw (2,0) rectangle (4,3);
\draw (4,0) rectangle (6,3);
\draw (2,3)--(3,4.5)--(4,3);
\draw (2,0)--(3,-1.5)--(4,0);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Name the solid that folds up from this net.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.55]
\draw (2,0) rectangle (5,2);
\draw (2,2) rectangle (5,4);
\draw (2,4) rectangle (5,6);
\draw (2,6) rectangle (5,8);
\draw (0,2) rectangle (2,4);
\draw (5,2) rectangle (7,4);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Name the solid that folds up from this net.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.8]
\draw (1,0) rectangle (2,1);
\draw (1,1) rectangle (2,2);
\draw (1,2) rectangle (2,3);
\draw (1,3) rectangle (2,4);
\draw (0,1) rectangle (1,2);
\draw (2,1) rectangle (3,2);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Name the solid that folds up from this net.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.7]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (1,2);
\draw (1,0) rectangle (2,2);
\draw (2,0) rectangle (3,2);
\draw (3,0) rectangle (4,2);
\draw (4,0) rectangle (5,2);
\draw (5,0) rectangle (6,2);
\draw (0,2)--(1,2)--(1.5,2.866)--(1,3.732)--(0,3.732)--(-0.5,2.866)--cycle;
\draw (0,0)--(1,0)--(1.5,-0.866)--(1,-1.732)--(0,-1.732)--(-0.5,-0.866)--cycle;
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Explain why this diagram is **not** the net of a triangular prism.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.7]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (2,3);
\draw (2,0) rectangle (4,3);
\draw (0,3)--(1,4.5)--(2,3);
\draw (0,0)--(1,-1.5)--(2,0);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

